Subject: api: run host imports on the coroutine stack when suspension is
 enabled

The import trampolines switch every host call to the OS thread's stack
through `on_host_stack`, which is what stops a syscall from suspending
the coroutine: the wait would be on a stack the coroutine does not own.
With suspension enabled the trampolines call the host function directly
on the coroutine stack; otherwise they behave as before.

This trades the isolation of host frames from guest-controlled stack
depth for suspendable syscalls: a stack overflow inside an import is
reported as a Wasm trap, and the host sizes the coroutine stacks for its
imports. Because an import can now be resumed on a different OS thread,
every access to the store-context thread-local goes through a function
that is never inlined; see wasmer-vm's `trap/suspend.rs`.

